name brown-tagged
match c[a-z][0-9][0-9]
format brown_tagged
content word tag
# Words share canonical content; the sentence is its words, and the tags laid along it are no claim of its own.
thing token word
thing sentence of token
thing paragraph of sentence
# A tag is the Brown Corpus's (nn-tl, as the corpus writes it in lower case), a key of the highway's brown tagset. Its
# crosswalk edge (NLTK's en-brown.map, carried to UD) reaches the universal part of speech the word is said to be, a
# value of upos as UD's treebanks say theirs: [County, NOUN]. The tag as written stays in the file and in
# [[brown, nn-tl], denotes, NOUN]; a tag the highway does not list is said, never taken for a part of speech.
type tag upos crosswalk brown
value upos tag
attest token tag
